---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — Ayomiposi Sotomi"
  description="Final-year Cybersecurity student. Freelance web developer. Security-minded human."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl lg:max-w-4xl px-6 py-20">
    <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl font-medium text-text md:text-5xl">
      About Me
    </h1>

    <div class="prose prose-neutral mt-10 max-w-none">
      <p>
        I'm Ayomiposi Sotomi — final-year Cybersecurity student, freelance
        web developer, and someone who'd rather learn a system by taking it
        apart than by reading about it. I'm based in Nigeria, the only home
        I've known, and I'm studying at the Federal University of
        Technology, Akure (FUTA).
      </p>
      <p>
        My focus is defensive security — the kind of work that goes into
        keeping systems standing rather than breaking them. Alongside that,
        I do freelance web development, and I run a homelab: currently a
        Docker-based media and automation stack, soon moving to a dedicated
        Proxmox server. Self-hosting things is still the fastest way I know
        to actually understand them. Longer term, I'd like to start a
        cybersecurity consulting firm.
      </p>
      <p>
        Growing up, the harder lessons weren't technical — they were about
        expectation. Hit one goal and there's already a next one waiting,
        and it's easy to keep chasing that without ever deciding for
        yourself what's enough. Learning to say no was most of the fix.
        That's part of why I value self-expression as much as I do, and why
        I try to be patient with people rather than quick to judge them.
      </p>
      <p>
        This site is where all of that lives in one place — occasional
        essays on whatever's been sitting in my head, homelab and project
        write-ups, and a running "Now" page — instead of scattered across
        Substack, GitHub, and social media. I don't think of myself as a
        writer exactly; mostly I write about my own thoughts and the small,
        ordinary things I notice day to day.
      </p>
      <p>
        It's meant to be a quiet garden rather than a portfolio — somewhere
        that shows the process, not just the finished, polished output.
        Half-built homelab experiments get written up here too, not just the
        wins.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you want to see what I'm building or get in touch, find me on{' '}
        <a href="https://github.com/BlackJRoot" class="text-link hover:text-accent">GitHub</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>